% External Breast Prostheses: LCD L33317 and its Policy Article A52478 (DME
% MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le
% (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states
% when a claim for an external breast prosthesis — a mastectomy form
% (L8020), a silicone or equal prosthesis (L8030), a nipple prosthesis
% (L8032), a bra with integrated prosthesis (L8001, L8002) — for the
% garment with mastectomy form (L8015) or for a mastectomy bra (L8000) is
% REASONABLE AND NECESSARY. The benefit is not durable medical equipment:
% the Policy Article places external breast prostheses under the Prosthetic
% Devices benefit of Social Security Act §1861(s)(8), so no condition on the
% place of use applies. The prosthesis with integral adhesive (L8031) and
% the custom fabricated prosthesis (L8035) are in scope and in the benefit
% but the LCD denies them as not reasonable and necessary: no rule covers
% them.
%
% The coverage criteria:
%   1. a mastectomy — the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is in the
%      Article's ICD-10 table (sources/icd10/A52478_icd10_covered.csv, 49
%      rows, loaded as the table breast_prostheses_icd10; its one group,
%      group 1, serves every code of the policy);
%   2. one prosthesis per side for the useful lifetime of the prosthesis
%      (two, one per side, after bilateral mastectomies): the useful
%      lifetime of each kind is the Article's, as days — 2 years is 730
%      days for a silicone prosthesis, 6 months 183 days for a fabric, foam
%      or fiber filled prosthesis (the mastectomy form), 3 months 91 days
%      for a nipple prosthesis — read from the table
%      breast_prostheses_lifetime; the side of the item and the prostheses
%      previously furnished for that side are facts of the record;
%   3. the exceptions: a prosthesis of the same type replaced at any time
%      when lost or irreparably damaged (not ordinary wear and tear: the
%      record fact says so), a prosthesis of a different type at any time
%      when a change in the medical condition requires it;
%   4. the garment with mastectomy form (L8015) for the postoperative period
%      before a permanent prosthesis or as an alternative to a bra and
%      prosthesis — the two uses are the only uses of the garment, so it is
%      covered for a beneficiary who has had a mastectomy;
%   5. the mastectomy bra (L8000) for a beneficiary who has a covered form
%      (L8020) or silicone prosthesis (L8030) held in its pocket — the bra
%      is an accessory of the prosthesis (the shared template).
% One finding is a judgment: "change in medical condition requires
% different type" (criterion 3: "a change in the patient's medical condition
% necessitating a different type of item").
%
% The payment conditions the Article adds (its "Policy specific
% documentation requirements"), in section remedy: the diagnosis code on
% each claim, and for a different type of prosthesis a new order explaining
% the need for it.
%
% Not modelled: the RT/LT modifiers and the billing of bilateral items on
% two claim lines (billing rules); the adhesive skin support (A4280), whose
% coverage neither text states; that documentation by a prosthetist is part
% of the medical record (how the record is read, not a criterion). The
% HCPCS code of the nipple prosthesis, L8032, is not named in either text:
% the Article gives the useful lifetime of "a nipple prostheses" and the
% code is the one that describes it.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    the side of *an item* is *a side*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* was furnished a breast prosthesis of code *a code* for side *a side* on *a date*; undefined.
    *an item* replaces a breast prosthesis of the same type that was lost or irreparably damaged; undefined.
    *an item* is a different type of breast prosthesis from the one previously furnished; undefined.
    the order for *an item* explains the need for a different type of breast prosthesis; undefined.
    the pocket of *an item* is used to hold *a device*; undefined.
    % the codes and the tables
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table breast_prostheses_icd10.
    the useful lifetime of a breast prosthesis of code *a code* is *a number* days under table breast_prostheses_lifetime.
    % derived
    *an item* is a breast prosthesis.
    *a beneficiary* has had a mastectomy.
    *a claim* is within the useful lifetime of the prosthesis.
    *a beneficiary* was furnished a breast prosthesis for side *a side* within its useful lifetime before *a date*.
    the new order requirement is met for *an item*.

% The Article's ICD-10 table: the diagnoses of a mastectomy (group 1, the
% only group; the CSV columns bind to the template's arguments in order:
% code, group, article, description).
the table breast_prostheses_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52478_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

% The useful lifetime of each kind of prosthesis (Policy Article A52478), in
% days: 2 years is 730 days, 6 months 183 days, 3 months 91 days.
the table breast_prostheses_lifetime is, with unique match, with provenance Policy Article A52478,
        confer "Replacement sooner than the useful lifetime because of ordinary wear and tear will be denied as noncovered":
    code    | days | confer
    "L8030" | 730  | "The useful lifetime expectancy for silicone breast prostheses is 2 years"
    "L8020" | 183  | "For fabric, foam, or fiber filled breast prostheses, the useful lifetime expectancy is 6 months"
    "L8032" | 91   | "The useful lifetime expectancy for a nipple prostheses is 3 months"

the knowledge base breast prostheses includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base breast prostheses includes:

LCD L33317 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33317".
the text of LCD L33317 is at "sources/lcd/L33317.txt".
Policy Article A52478 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52478".
the text of Policy Article A52478 is at "sources/article/A52478.txt".

% What a breast prosthesis is: the form and the silicone prosthesis (the
% LCD), the bras with integrated prosthesis (the Article's coding
% guidelines), the nipple prosthesis (the Article's useful lifetime).
rule breast_prosthesis_form with provenance LCD L33317,
        confer "a covered mastectomy form (L8020) or silicone (or equal) breast prosthesis (L8030)":
an item is a breast prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L8020", "L8030"].

rule breast_prosthesis_integrated with provenance Policy Article A52478,
        confer "Codes L8001 and L8002 describe a bra with integrated breast prosthesis, either unilateral or bilateral, respectively":
an item is a breast prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L8001", "L8002"].

rule breast_prosthesis_nipple with provenance Policy Article A52478,
        confer "The useful lifetime expectancy for a nipple prostheses is 3 months":
an item is a breast prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "L8032".

% A prosthesis furnished for the same side whose useful lifetime has not
% run out by the date of service: a device of this model.
rule breast_previous:
a beneficiary was furnished a breast prosthesis for side a side within its useful lifetime before a date
    if the beneficiary was furnished a breast prosthesis of code a code for side the side on an other date
    and the useful lifetime of a breast prosthesis of code the code is a number days under table breast_prostheses_lifetime
    and the date is an other number days after the other date
    and the other number >= 0
    and the other number < the number.

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides: the prostheses, the garment and the bra
% the texts name, including the two the LCD denies.
rule breast_codes with provenance Policy Article A52478,
        confer "The diagnosis code must be included on each claim for the prosthesis or related item":
the policy for code a code is breast_prostheses
    if the code is in ["L8000", "L8001", "L8002", "L8015", "L8020", "L8030", "L8031", "L8032", "L8035"].

section applicability is:

% The benefit: not durable medical equipment but the Prosthetic Devices
% benefit of Social Security Act §1861(s)(8).
rule breast_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52478,
        confer "External Breast Prostheses are covered under the Prosthetic Devices benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(8))":
the benefit category of code a code is prosthetic devices
    if the policy for code the code is breast_prostheses.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The claims: a prosthesis, its replacement, the garment, the bra.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule breast_covered with provenance LCD L33317,
        confer "A breast prosthesis is covered for a patient who has had a mastectomy":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a breast prosthesis
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has had a mastectomy
    and the claim is within the useful lifetime of the prosthesis.

rule breast_replacement_lost with provenance LCD L33317,
        confer "An external breast prosthesis of the same type can be replaced at any time if it is lost or is irreparably damaged":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a breast prosthesis
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has had a mastectomy
    and the item replaces a breast prosthesis of the same type that was lost or irreparably damaged.

rule breast_different_type with provenance LCD L33317,
        confer "An external breast prosthesis of a different type can be covered at any time if there is a change in the patient's medical condition necessitating a different type of item":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a breast prosthesis
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has had a mastectomy
    and the item is a different type of breast prosthesis from the one previously furnished
    and the finding change in medical condition requires different type about the beneficiary is established.

rule breast_garment with provenance LCD L33317,
        confer "An external breast prosthesis garment, with mastectomy form (L8015) is covered for use in the postoperative period prior to a permanent breast prosthesis or as an alternative to a mastectomy bra and breast prosthesis":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "L8015"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has had a mastectomy.

rule breast_bra with provenance LCD L33317,
        confer "A mastectomy bra (L8000) is covered for a patient who has a covered mastectomy form (L8020) or silicone (or equal) breast prosthesis (L8030) when the pocket of the bra is used to hold the form/prosthesis":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "L8000"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the HCPCS code of the device is a code
    and the code is in ["L8020", "L8030"]
    and the device is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has had a mastectomy
    and the pocket of the item is used to hold the device.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The criteria: the mastectomy, the useful lifetime.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Criterion 1: the diagnosis code on the claim is one of the Article's.
rule breast_mastectomy with provenance LCD L33317,
        confer "(Refer to the ICD-10 code list in the LCD-related Policy Article for applicable diagnoses.)":
a beneficiary has had a mastectomy
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A52478" as a description under table breast_prostheses_icd10.

% Criterion 2: one prosthesis per side for the useful lifetime — no
% prosthesis furnished for that side is still within its useful lifetime on
% the date of service (a prosthesis whose lifetime the Article does not
% state, a bra with integrated prosthesis, counts for nothing).
rule breast_lifetime with provenance LCD L33317,
        confer "The Medicare program will pay for only one breast prosthesis per side for the useful lifetime of the prosthesis":
a claim is within the useful lifetime of the prosthesis
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the side of the item is a side
    and the date of service of the claim is a date
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary was furnished a breast prosthesis for side the side within its useful lifetime before the date.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment (Policy Article A52478, "Policy
% specific documentation requirements"): the diagnosis code on the claim,
% and the new order for a different type of prosthesis.
rule breast_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52478,
        confer "The diagnosis code must be included on each claim for the prosthesis or related item":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is breast_prostheses
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and the new order requirement is met for the item.

rule breast_new_order with provenance Policy Article A52478,
        confer "If the patient's medical condition changes, this should be documented by the patient's treating practitioner submitting a new order which explains the need for a different type of breast prosthesis":
the new order requirement is met for an item
    if the item is a different type of breast prosthesis from the one previously furnished
    and the order for the item explains the need for a different type of breast prosthesis.

rule breast_same_type with provenance Policy Article A52478,
        confer "If the patient's medical condition changes, this should be documented by the patient's treating practitioner submitting a new order which explains the need for a different type of breast prosthesis":
the new order requirement is met for an item
    if the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a different type of breast prosthesis from the one previously furnished.
